WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.972
Step 1. Find the Observation Interpretation section.

1.2
00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:09.554
Care uses these rules to interpret each result, for example as Normal or High.

1.3
00:00:09.554 --> 00:00:12.845
The section is below Basic Information.

2.1
00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.542
Step 2. Add a rule. Select Add Interpretation.

2.2
00:00:16.542 --> 00:00:23.188
Care opens the interpretation panel, and the new rule starts with one empty range.

3.1
00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:26.614
Step 3. Name the rule. The title is optional.

3.2
00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:32.690
Type a short title in the box at the top of the panel, for example Adult range.

4.1
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:39.018
Step 4. Add conditions. In the Conditions section, select Add, then select a metric,

4.2
00:00:39.018 --> 00:00:42.346
an operation and a value, such as patient age.

4.3
00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:50.738
The rule applies only when all its conditions match.

5.1
00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:52.806
Step 5. Add the ranges.

5.2
00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:57.943
Enter the Display text, such as Normal, and a Min, a Max or both.

5.3
00:00:57.943 --> 00:01:15.424
A range includes both its ends, and ranges must not overlap.

6.1
00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:18.986
Step 6. Turn on the fallback. This is optional.

6.2
00:01:18.986 --> 00:01:24.701
Care uses the fallback when the rule applies but no range holds the value.

7.1
00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:27.424
Step 7. Save the rule. Select Save.

7.2
00:01:27.424 --> 00:01:31.170
It is available once the rule has at least one range.

7.3
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.839
Care adds the rule after the existing rules in the section.

8.1
00:01:35.839 --> 00:01:38.734
Step 8. Review the order of the rules.

8.2
00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:42.700
Care uses only the first rule whose conditions all match.

8.3
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.210
Put the rules with conditions first, and a rule without conditions last.

9.1
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.310
Step 9. Save the observation definition.

9.2
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:55.514
Select Create on the create form, or Save on the edit form.

9.3
00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:59.576
Care stores the rules only when you save the form.
